WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.328 --> 00:00:15.851
When the ghost reached his secret chamber in the castle, he leaned up against a moonbeam to catch

2
00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:16.332
his breath.

3
00:00:17.372 --> 00:00:20.575
"Never before in three hundred years have I ever been so insulted!"

4
00:00:21.035 --> 00:00:21.615
he gasped.

5
00:00:22.636 --> 00:00:27.199
He thought back to when he had grinned ghoulishly in Lady Bracknell's mirror and had turned her hair

6
00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:28.040
as white as ash.

7
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:34.124
He smiled as he remembered the three hysterical housemaids who had found him bowling in the graveyard behind

8
00:00:34.164 --> 00:00:36.665
the castle, using his head for a ball.

9
00:00:37.966 --> 00:00:42.349
For a while he recalled, like a famous actor, all his great performances of the past.

10
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:47.533
Thinking about the costumes he had worn and the screams and moans he had uttered cheered him a

11
00:00:47.573 --> 00:00:53.336
little. He took off his chains and passed the night watching the dim shadows cast by the moonlight

12
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:55.478
creep across the stone floor.

13
00:00:56.699 --> 00:01:00.261
When the Otis family met at breakfast, they discussed the ghost at some length.

14
00:01:00.781 --> 00:01:04.884
"I think it was quite rude of the ghost not to use the lubricator I offered," said Mr.

15
00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:10.347
Otis. "Still," said Virginia, "I don't think it was very polite to throw pillows at him."

16
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:14.369
At this, the twins looked at each other and burst into laughter.

17
00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:19.572
"Stop that, you two, and keep your slingshots off the dining table," said Mrs.

18
00:01:19.672 --> 00:01:25.516
Otis. "I think we must simply take his chains from him so he doesn't bother us again," suggested

19
00:01:25.576 --> 00:01:31.455
Washington. For the rest of the week, however, the only ghostly occurrence was the bloodstain in the library.

20
00:01:32.356 --> 00:01:35.298
Washington cleaned it up every morning, and every night Mr.

21
00:01:35.398 --> 00:01:39.701
Otis locked the library doors, but in the morning it always reappeared.

22
00:01:40.681 --> 00:01:42.663
Strangely enough, it kept changing colors.

23
00:01:43.663 --> 00:01:48.847
It started out as blood red, changed to royal purple, and then became flame orange for a few

24
00:01:48.887 --> 00:01:51.629
days. The twins thought this was great fun.

25
00:01:52.469 --> 00:01:53.390
Washington and Mr.

26
00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.572
Otis even started laying bets on the stain's color before bed.

27
00:01:57.376 --> 00:02:02.500
Virginia was the only one who seemed upset, however, and the morning they all came down to find

28
00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:05.403
the stain a bright emerald green, she nearly cried.

29
00:02:06.563 --> 00:02:11.407
On Sunday night, shortly after everyone had gone to bed, there was a loud crash in the hall.

30
00:02:12.348 --> 00:02:13.709
"What on earth is going on?"

31
00:02:14.049 --> 00:02:14.510
said Mr.

32
00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.112
Otis, stepping out into the hallway with a candle.

33
00:02:17.953 --> 00:02:22.376
Virginia opened her door and saw the twins rush past carrying their slingshots.

34
00:02:23.257 --> 00:02:26.900
When she caught up, the rest of the family was gathered at the top of the stairs.

35
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.744
Looking down, she saw the suit of armor that had stood at the bottom of the stairway scattered

36
00:02:31.804 --> 00:02:32.444
over the floor.

37
00:02:33.545 --> 00:02:37.609
And sitting in the tall wooden chair against the wall was the Canterville ghost rubbing his knee.

38
00:02:38.249 --> 00:02:42.613
The twins immediately loaded their slingshots and accurately fired two small stones.

39
00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:48.758
In a rage, the ghost flew up the stairs at the family, spread his skeleton arms wide, and

40
00:02:48.798 --> 00:02:50.820
let out his loudest, most demonic groan.

41
00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.162
"Oh my," said Mrs.

42
00:02:53.242 --> 00:02:55.304
Otis, "he doesn't sound well at all.

43
00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.722
I think I'll go fetch him some cough syrup from the kitchen."

44
00:02:59.783 --> 00:03:03.186
But before she could start down the stairs, the ghost blew out Mr.

45
00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:05.448
Otis' candle and vanished in the dark.

46
00:03:06.389 --> 00:03:11.533
Just as the candle went out, Virginia thought she saw a sad expression pass over the ghost's face.

47
00:03:12.514 --> 00:03:16.077
As the ghost snuck through the dark corridors, he wiped a tear from his eye.

48
00:03:16.897 --> 00:03:19.019
He had planned such a terrifying surprise!

49
00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:24.323
He had wanted to parade through their bedrooms in the ancient suit of armor while brandishing a gleaming

50
00:03:25.292 --> 00:03:27.053
sword─but it had all come to nothing.

51
00:03:27.533 --> 00:03:31.836
He had been so worried about a sneak attack from behind that he hadn't watched what he was

52
00:03:31.876 --> 00:03:36.720
doing. He had knocked over the armor with his knee, and it had all collapsed on top of

53
00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:41.703
him. Now he just wanted to slink off to his room and bandage his wound with cobwebs.

54
00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:47.667
But first, he bravely and quietly went to the library and made sure the stain was ready for

55
00:03:47.707 --> 00:03:54.511
morning. Afterward he sat among the ashes in the fireplace─one of his favorite places in the castle─and made

56
00:03:54.551 --> 00:03:55.352
a solemn vow.

57
00:03:56.244 --> 00:04:00.265
"I will have my vengeance on this ill-mannered, awful family," he promised.

58
00:04:01.185 --> 00:04:06.767
The next night a violent storm thrashed the castle windows with rain, and the wind howled about the

59
00:04:06.807 --> 00:04:08.407
turrets like a lost soul.

60
00:04:09.308 --> 00:04:11.568
It was just the kind of weather the ghost loved.

61
00:04:12.509 --> 00:04:16.610
"It is time to put the fear of the supernatural into these people," he said as he looked

62
00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:17.450
through his wardrobe.

63
00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:23.452
He picked out a long winding-sheet the color of gravestone and a thread-worn jacket with bloodstains.

64
00:04:23.952 --> 00:04:24.892
He planned his attack.

65
00:04:25.972 --> 00:04:30.576
"I'll start by scaring the twins out of their beds in the form of a green, icy-cold corpse,"

66
00:04:30.896 --> 00:04:31.297
he thought.

67
00:04:31.317 --> 00:04:37.622
"Then I'll pass through the wall into Washington's room, where I'll moan hideously and stab my chest with

68
00:04:37.682 --> 00:04:38.122
a dagger."

69
00:04:39.203 --> 00:04:39.604
For Mr.

70
00:04:39.624 --> 00:04:39.984
and Mrs.

71
00:04:40.084 --> 00:04:45.369
Otis, he planned to haunt their dreams with visions of hellfire, but he didn't quite know what he

72
00:04:45.389 --> 00:04:46.490
would do for Virginia.

73
00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.612
She had never insulted him and seemed quite gentle.

74
00:04:50.513 --> 00:04:53.756
"Perhaps I'll just groan as I pass by her door," he thought.

75
00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.102
At half past ten, he heard the family go to bed.

76
00:04:57.982 --> 00:05:03.085
For a little while, wild shrieks of laughter came from the twins' room, but eventually the only noise

77
00:05:03.145 --> 00:05:04.406
was the storm outside.

78
00:05:05.246 --> 00:05:10.410
Just before he started out, he decided that, for an added touch of horror, he would leave his

79
00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:11.210
head behind.

80
00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:16.093
He glided through the walls of the castle like an evil shadow until he stood just outside the

81
00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:16.673
twins' room.

82
00:05:17.194 --> 00:05:18.534
The door was slightly ajar.

83
00:05:19.415 --> 00:05:24.763
Wishing to make a dramatic entrance, he screamed his favorite sixteenth-century curses and flung open the door.

84
00:05:25.703 --> 00:05:30.747
A heavy jug of water, which had been cunningly balanced on top of the door, fell heavily onto

85
00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:32.668
the ghost and soaked him through to the bones.

86
00:05:33.549 --> 00:05:36.591
The twins, sitting up in their beds, were laughing uproariously.

87
00:05:37.511 --> 00:05:40.213
The ghost got up on one knee in the cold, wet puddle.

88
00:05:40.954 --> 00:05:45.257
When he saw the twins reach for their pillows, he let out a cry that sounded more frightened

89
00:05:45.477 --> 00:05:48.079
than ghostly and escaped through the floor in a flash.

90
00:05:49.319 --> 00:05:51.605
That night the ghost came down with a cold.

91
00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:55.866
He was just glad that he hadn't brought his head or the shock to his system might have

92
00:05:55.886 --> 00:05:56.687
been far worse.

93
00:05:57.587 --> 00:05:59.908
As it was, his nerves were completely shot.

94
00:06:00.408 --> 00:06:02.589
He decided to give up the stain in the library.

95
00:06:03.509 --> 00:06:08.271
Obviously the Otis family had no appreciation for spiritual phenomena and didn't deserve it.

96
00:06:09.332 --> 00:06:14.554
Nonetheless he did have a solemn obligation to appear on the terraced balcony twice a week and to

97
00:06:14.594 --> 00:06:17.015
tread the corridors in chains every Sunday at midnight.

98
00:06:17.955 --> 00:06:22.242
It is quite true that his life had been evil, but on the other hand, he was very

99
00:06:22.302 --> 00:06:24.643
responsible when it came to his supernatural duties.

100
00:06:25.564 --> 00:06:28.366
And after three centuries, he wasn't going to give up now.

101
00:06:29.247 --> 00:06:33.370
When he had recovered a little from his cold, he snuck back to the hallway outside Mr.

102
00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:33.751
and Mrs.

103
00:06:33.891 --> 00:06:34.611
Otis' room.

104
00:06:35.492 --> 00:06:39.796
With a heavy sigh, he stooped to pick up the bottle of Rising Sun Lubricator from under the

105
00:06:39.816 --> 00:06:44.860
table. Back in his room, he found that if he applied the oil to his chains and removed

106
00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:49.383
his big leather boots, he could haunt the castle hallways as quietly as a
